      "q_source": "stage2_test_predictions.csv",
      "step_number": 2,
      "text": "Step 2: Use the binomial probability formula to calculate the probability of finding treasure on exactly 4 out of 7 islands. The formula is given by $P(X = k) = \\binom{n}{k} p^k (1-p)^{n-k}$, where $n$ is the total number of trials (islands), $k$ is the number of successes (islands with treasure), $p$ is the probability of success on a single trial, and $\\binom{n}{k}$ is the binomial coefficient representing the number of ways to choose $k$ successes from $n$ trials.",
      "z": -0.38909666330601334
    },
    {
      "aligned_char_end": 1043,
